.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tokenbooth-login 1  "tokenbooth 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
tokenbooth\-login \- Open the login window and print the token it captures
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtokenbooth login\fR [\fB\-\-socket\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-pidvault\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-pidvault\-mount\fR] [\fB\-\-to\-vault\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open the login window and print the token it captures
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fI<SOCKET>\fR [default: /run/tokenbooth/sock]
The daemon\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Log navigations and cookie names (never values) to stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print {"token": ..., "expires": ...} instead of the bare token
.TP
\fB\-\-pidvault\-socket\fR \fI<PIDVAULT_SOCKET>\fR [default: /run/pidvault.sock]
pidvault\*(Aqs control socket, which the daemon asks whether this shell is unlocked
.TP
\fB\-\-pidvault\-mount\fR \fI<PIDVAULT_MOUNT>\fR [default: /run/pidvault]
Where pidvault shows unlocked vaults; each profile\*(Aqs key is kept in its vault there
.TP
\fB\-\-to\-vault\fR
Write the token to tokens/NAME in the profile\*(Aqs vault instead of printing it, where only processes the vault is unlocked for can read it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
The profile
